            title: "Conversation and token totals",
            body:
              "Track native-chat messages and turns plus available input, output, cache, and reasoning token metadata from the session or summary baseline.",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        title: "Persistence and background work",
        intro: "Keep session state and conversation history available across app restarts.",
        items: [
          {
            title: "Conversation UUID tracking",
            body: "Track Claude, Codex, and Antigravity conversation UUIDs per session and suggest resume on focus.",
          },
          {
            title: "History tab",
            body: "Browse project transcript history in the right panel and double-click to resume in a new terminal.",
          },
          {
            title: "Background sessions",
            body:
              "PTY sessions keep running after quit or restart. Reopen the app to restore the screen, and manage Kill, Restore, and Forget from Services settings.",
          },
          {
            title: "Status bar controls",
            body: "Check and control background session state from the status bar icon and dropdown.",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        title: "Control session",
        intro: "An advanced automation mode where one agent session can operate other sessions in the same project.",
        items: [
          {
            title: "Remote session control",
            body: "Send input, read screens, create sessions, select targets, and close sessions from another session.",
          },
          {
            title: "Quick start",
            body:
              "Start with ⌘⌥⇧T, the project header Bot icon, or New control session in the command palette. From an existing terminal, run acorn-ipc promote-self to promote that session.",
          },
          {
            title: "Platform support",
            body: "Supported on macOS and Linux. Windows is not currently supported.",
          },
        ],
        link: { label: "Control session docs", href: links.controlDocs },
      },
      {
        title: "Right panel",
        intro: "Code, GitHub, and Agents tabs keep review and coordination work near the terminal.",
        items: [
          {
            title: "Code: Files / Staged / Commits",
            body:
              "File tree, search, Git status, staged changes, commits, and a Diff modal. File references from the terminal can open in the code viewer.",
          },
          {
            title: "GitHub: PRs / Issues / Actions",
            body:
              "Browse PRs and issues with detail views for conversations, commits, checks, and files. Create, edit, or delete issue and PR comments, toggle PR tasks, and generate merge messages with AI.",
          },
          {
            title: "GitHub Actions",
            body: "Inspect workflow runs and filter by workflow without switching to the browser.",
          },
          {
            title: "Agents: Activity / History / Todos",
            body:
              "Session notifications, transcript history, and Claude Code todo lists parsed from TodoWrite events.",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        title: "Code, diff, and alerts",
        intro: "Supporting tools for reading code, reviewing changes, and tracking session events.",
        items: [
          {
            title: "File Explorer and code viewer",
            body: "Search filenames and content with regex, case, include, and exclude filters; toggle dotfiles and gitignored files; rename, trash, copy paths, and attach files to agents. The code viewer adds syntax highlighting, in-file search, and Markdown source/preview modes.",
          },
          {
            title: "Media viewer",
            body: "Preview image, video, audio, and PDF files inside the app. Images include zoom in, zoom out, and reset controls.",
          },
          {
            title: "Diff viewer",
            body: "Review changes in unified or split mode before committing or merging.",
          },
          {
            title: "Activity center",
            body:
              "Collect waiting, done, and failed events in the right panel and status bar, with native notification toggles and retention settings.",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        title: "Settings and system status",
        intro: "Tune the app to your workflow and macOS environment.",
        items: [
          {
            title: "UI and terminal settings",
            body: "Set language, UI scale, theme, background image, the default Pane or Kanban view, and popover behavior. Tune terminal font fallbacks and presets, size, weight, spacing, line height, antialiasing, and resident terminal limits.",
          },
          {
            title: "Custom shortcuts",
            body: "Record shortcuts directly, detect conflicts, and reset individual bindings or the complete shortcut map.",
          },
          {
            title: "AI providers and external tools",
            body:
              "Use Claude Code, Codex, or Antigravity for Acorn's native AI features. Inside sessions, you can still run Ollama, llm, or custom CLIs directly, and configure an external editor command.",
          },
          {
            title: "Cleanup tools",
            body: "Manage background sessions, keep-awake behavior, close warnings, orphan worktrees, caches, and macOS protected-folder permission checks.",
          },
          {
            title: "Status bar",
            body:
              "Memory and process breakdown, current worktree branch, GitHub account badge, active Claude or Codex token usage, background sessions, and multi-input state.",
          },
          {
            title: "Auto-update",
            body: "Detect new macOS releases, show an update banner, and let the user choose when to apply it. The About tab also shows GitHub release notes for the current version.",
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
    shortcutsTitle: "Core shortcuts",
    shortcuts: [
      ["Command palette", "⌘P"],
      ["New session / isolated / control", "⌘T / ⌘⌥T / ⌘⌥⇧T"],
      ["New project", "⌘⇧N"],
      ["Split pane vertical / horizontal", "⌘D / ⌘⇧D"],
      ["Equalize pane sizes", "⌘⌥E"],
      ["Close tab", "⌘W"],
      ["Focus sidebar / main / right panel", "⌘1 / ⌘2 / ⌘3"],
      ["Toggle sidebar / right panel", "⌘B / ⌘J"],
      ["Toggle multi-input", "⌘⌥I"],
      ["Next / previous session", "Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+⇧+Tab"],
      ["Latest needs-input session", "Ctrl+⌥]"],
      ["Clear terminal", "⌘K"],
      ["Settings", "⌘,"],
    ],
  },
} as const;

const c = copy[lang];
---

<section class="featureHero">
  <div class="container featureHero__inner">
    <div class="featureHero__copy reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">{c.eyebrow}</span>
      <h1>{c.title}</h1>
      <p>{c.lead}</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="featureHero__media reveal">
      <img src={asset("screenshots/workspace.png")} alt={c.screenshotAlt} width="1600" height="1000" />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="featureQuick">
  <div class="container featureQuick__inner reveal">
    <h2>{c.quickTitle}</h2>
    <ul>
      {c.quickItems.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="featureCatalog">
  <div class="container featureCatalog__inner">
    {
      c.groups.map((group, groupIndex) => (
        <article class="featureGroup reveal">
          <header class="featureGroup__head">
            <span>{String(groupIndex + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
            <div>
              <h2>{group.title}</h2>
              <p>{group.intro}</p>
            </div>
          </header>

          <div class="featureGroup__items">
            {group.items.map((item) => (
              <section class="featureItem">
                <h3>{item.title}</h3>
                <p>{item.body}</p>
              </section>
            ))}
          </div>

          {"link" in group && group.link && (
            <a class="featureGroup__link" href={group.link.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              {group.link.label}
            </a>
          )}
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shortcuts">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="shortcuts__inner reveal">
      <h2>{c.shortcutsTitle}</h2>
      <div class="shortcuts__list">
        {
          c.shortcuts.map(([label, keys]) => (
            <div class="shortcut">
              <span>{label}</span>
              <code>{keys}</code>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .featureHero {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 2.2rem + 4vw, 6rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .featureHero__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(280px, 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 4vw, 4.5rem);
  }
  .featureHero h1 {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    max-width: 14ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .featureHero p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    max-width: 42ch;
  }
  .featureHero__media {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .featureHero__media img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .featureQuick {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 1.3rem + 3vw, 3.5rem);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .featureQuick__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(160px, 0.24fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 3vw, 3rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .featureQuick h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
  }
  .featureQuick ul {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .featureQuick li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .featureQuick li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.68em;
    width: 0.42rem;
    height: 0.42rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .featureCatalog {
    padding-block: var(--space-section);
  }
  .featureCatalog__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 5rem);
  }
  .featureGroup {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 0.35fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 3vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(2.25rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 4rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .featureGroup:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }
  .featureGroup__head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    align-content: start;
  }
  .featureGroup__head > span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .featureGroup h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .featureGroup__head p {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .featureGroup__items {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.35rem 1.6rem;
  }
  .featureItem {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .featureItem h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .featureItem p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.58;
  }
  .featureGroup__link {
    grid-column: 2;
    justify-self: start;
    margin-top: -0.25rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .featureGroup__link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .shortcuts {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-section);
  }
  .shortcuts__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 0.28fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 3vw, 3rem);
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 3.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .shortcuts h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
  }
  .shortcuts__list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }
  .shortcut {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(120px, auto);
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-bottom: 0.65rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--border) 70%, transparent);
  }
  .shortcut span {
    min-width: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .shortcut code {
    justify-self: end;
    max-width: 100%;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-align: right;
    white-space: normal;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .featureHero__inner,
    .featureQuick__inner,
    .featureGroup,
    .shortcuts__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .featureHero h1,
    .featureHero p {
      max-width: none;
    }
    .featureGroup__link {
      grid-column: 1;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .featureQuick ul,
    .featureGroup__items {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .featureGroup__head {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    .shortcut {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }
    .shortcut code {
      justify-self: start;
      text-align: left;
    }
  }
</style>
